WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.534
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show,"
everybody.

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:03.567
Thank you for being here.

00:00:03.567 --> 00:00:04.567
Thank you for watching.

00:00:04.567 --> 00:00:06.767
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:06.767 --> 00:00:08.601
What a show we have
for you tonight.

00:00:08.601 --> 00:00:11.234
From the big summer blockbuster
"Top Gun: Maverick,"

00:00:11.234 --> 00:00:13.267
Jon Hamm is my guest tonight!
-Come on!

00:00:13.267 --> 00:00:17.601
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:17.601 --> 00:00:19.400
It is such a treat.
You all get to look

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:21.567
at a tall, handsome,
charming guy.

00:00:21.567 --> 00:00:23.167
And also, Jon Hamm is here.

00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:25.901
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Awesome.

00:00:25.901 --> 00:00:27.267
That's right,
"Top Gun: Maverick"

00:00:27.267 --> 00:00:29.601
is expected to be
the summer's biggest movie.

00:00:29.601 --> 00:00:31.334
It took 36 years
to make the sequel,

00:00:31.334 --> 00:00:33.000
so, if it does well enough,

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:35.000
they're going to finish
the trilogy in 2058.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.300
[ Laughter and applause ]
So, fingers crossed.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:39.501
Well, this is exciting --
today, after a two-year hiatus,

00:00:39.501 --> 00:00:42.200
Fleet Week returned
to New York City.

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:43.367
[ Cheering and applause ]
Fleet Week.

00:00:43.367 --> 00:00:44.033
I love it.

00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:49.133
I love it. What's better than
seeing a bunch of Navy SEALs

00:00:49.133 --> 00:00:50.467
infiltrate the M&amp;M store?

00:00:50.467 --> 00:00:52.834
[ Laughter ]
"I'm going in."

00:00:52.834 --> 00:00:54.367
Of course,
Fleet Week kicked off today

00:00:54.367 --> 00:00:57.234
with the parade of ships
up the Hudson River.

00:00:57.234 --> 00:00:58.934
At first I thought,
"Damn, the marketing

00:00:58.934 --> 00:01:00.267
for 'Top Gun' is insane."

00:01:00.267 --> 00:01:01.968
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:01.968 --> 00:01:05.100
Meanwhile, today is also
National Wine Day.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.767
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:09.067
-Oh, yeah!

00:01:09.067 --> 00:01:11.501
-Some people celebrated
by slowly pouring a glass,

00:01:11.501 --> 00:01:12.534
sniffing, and swirling,

00:01:12.534 --> 00:01:13.701
while others stuck a straw

00:01:13.701 --> 00:01:14.934
right through the Franzia bag,

00:01:14.934 --> 00:01:16.567
like an alcoholic Capri Sun.

00:01:16.567 --> 00:01:18.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:19.701
But, if wine isn't your thing,

00:01:19.701 --> 00:01:21.267
I saw that Miller Lite
is gearing up

00:01:21.267 --> 00:01:23.000
for the long weekend
with a brand-new

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.868
beer and barbecue combination.

00:01:24.868 --> 00:01:25.734
Take a look at this.

00:01:25.734 --> 00:01:27.067
-The American Brewing Company

00:01:27.067 --> 00:01:29.968
is introducing
Miller Lite Beercoal.

00:01:29.968 --> 00:01:34.234
It's the first ever
Miller Lite-infused charcoal.

00:01:34.234 --> 00:01:36.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.067 --> 00:01:38.501
-It's pretty amazing.
Now, my dad and my charcoal

00:01:38.501 --> 00:01:39.968
can both get lit
at the same time.

00:01:39.968 --> 00:01:41.267
-Oh.
-It's unbelievable.
Very interesting.

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:44.434
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:44.434 --> 00:01:46.367
The great thing about charcoal
made from Miller Lite is

00:01:46.367 --> 00:01:48.334
that there's enough alcohol
to get a flame going,

00:01:48.334 --> 00:01:50.501
but enough water to put it out,
you know what I'm saying?

00:01:50.501 --> 00:01:51.868
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.868 --> 00:01:54.701
Speaking of mashups,
Oreo and Ritz have teamed up

00:01:54.701 --> 00:01:57.100
to combine Ritz crackers
and Oreo cookies

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:58.634
into a limited edition snack.

00:01:58.634 --> 00:01:59.801
Here, take a look at this.

00:01:59.801 --> 00:02:01.767
[ Ewws and ohs ]

00:02:01.767 --> 00:02:03.067
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.067 --> 00:02:04.634
Seems kind of weird,
but that's actually not

00:02:04.634 --> 00:02:06.734
the strangest snack mashup.
I'll show you what I mean.

00:02:06.734 --> 00:02:11.067
For instance, Corn Nuts,
Kashi, and Fritos Chili Cheese

00:02:11.067 --> 00:02:13.501
teamed up to create...

00:02:13.501 --> 00:02:16.534
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:18.434 --> 00:02:23.200
Next up, Chef Boyardee teamed up
with Swedish Fish to create...

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:25.200
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:28.767
And, finally, Doritos teamed up
with Planters to create...

00:02:28.767 --> 00:02:30.467
[ Cheering and applause ]
There you go.
That's interesting.

00:02:30.467 --> 00:02:32.667
[ Rimshot ]
Interesting combo.
I think it'll work.

00:02:36.033 --> 00:02:38.834
Well, as I've mentioned before,
YouTube has a new feature

00:02:38.834 --> 00:02:41.467
where you can skip
the boring parts of a video

00:02:41.467 --> 00:02:43.167
and cut right to the good part.

00:02:43.167 --> 00:02:45.400
And I guess they also have
something similar on TikTok

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:47.100
and we tried it out
with some recent videos

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.601
people have posted.
For instance,

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:51.200
if you're watching a video,
you can skip this part...

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:54.634
♪♪

00:02:54.634 --> 00:02:56.100
...and go right to this...

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:58.133
♪♪

00:02:58.133 --> 00:03:01.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.901 --> 00:03:04.701
Let me give you
one more example.

00:03:04.701 --> 00:03:06.968
You can skip this part...

00:03:06.968 --> 00:03:08.434
-What's up, [bleep]?

00:03:08.434 --> 00:03:09.868
I'll show you how to Wutang.

00:03:11.334 --> 00:03:12.567
...and go right to this...

00:03:15.067 --> 00:03:18.100
[ Coughs ]
[ Ohs and applause ]

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:20.100
-Whoa! Whoa!

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:23.467
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:23.467 --> 00:03:25.000
-What?!

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:26.968
-I've never seen that.
-Never seen that before

00:03:26.968 --> 00:03:28.701
in my life, ever.
Never seen that.

00:03:28.701 --> 00:03:31.334
-Oh, my God.

00:03:31.334 --> 00:03:34.200
Ooh!
-Guys, some news from overseas.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:36.100
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:37.534
Some news from overseas --

00:03:37.534 --> 00:03:41.000
I saw that Nike is reportedly
leaving Russia permanently.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:42.868
[ Oohs ]
Yep, Nike is basically the same

00:03:42.868 --> 00:03:44.467
in Russia,
except the slogan is...

00:03:44.467 --> 00:03:45.901
[ Russian accent ]

00:03:45.901 --> 00:03:47.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.601 --> 00:03:49.734
Some more news here --
I read that, in an effort

00:03:49.734 --> 00:03:52.267
to lower gas prices,
the government is considering

00:03:52.267 --> 00:03:56.467
tapping into a rarely used
emergency diesel reserve.

00:03:56.467 --> 00:03:57.834
Check out this announcement.

00:03:57.834 --> 00:04:00.567
-Yo, it's Vin Diesel,
here to tell you
[ Laughter ]

00:04:00.567 --> 00:04:02.100
[ Ethereal "Battle Hymn
of the Republic" plays ]
about the diesel reserve.

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:04.634
The White House is taking care
of our cars

00:04:04.634 --> 00:04:06.767
because cars are family

00:04:06.767 --> 00:04:09.067
and we'll do anything
for our family,

00:04:09.067 --> 00:04:11.701
[ Laughter ]
just like we do anything
for our cars.

00:04:11.701 --> 00:04:13.400
We feed our families food

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:15.434
like we feed our cars gas.

00:04:15.434 --> 00:04:17.634
Opening the tank is like
opening your mouth

00:04:17.634 --> 00:04:20.033
and putting gas in is like food.

00:04:20.033 --> 00:04:22.467
[ Laughter ]
Think about different people
in your family.

00:04:22.467 --> 00:04:23.901
Some eat premium,

00:04:23.901 --> 00:04:25.634
but others eat unleaded.

00:04:25.634 --> 00:04:27.501
[ Laughter ]
And the gas station
is kind of like

00:04:27.501 --> 00:04:29.067
a car's Olive Garden.

00:04:29.067 --> 00:04:31.167
[ Laughter ]
And you know what they say
at Olive Garden...

00:04:33.934 --> 00:04:36.100
[ Laughter ]
Fill up and leave.

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:37.000
-Interesting, right?

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:40.033
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:04:43.167 --> 00:04:45.834
Well, this is going viral --
a raccoon in California

00:04:45.834 --> 00:04:48.367
is doing fine
after it got stuck in a roof.

00:04:48.367 --> 00:04:50.067
Check this out.

00:04:50.067 --> 00:04:52.534
[ Laughter and ohs ]

00:04:52.534 --> 00:04:54.767
Even worse, the ceiling fan
kept smacking it in the face.

00:04:54.767 --> 00:04:57.367
It's like, "Ouch, ouch,
ouch, ouch, ouch."

00:04:57.367 --> 00:04:58.667
[ Laughter ]

00:04:58.667 --> 00:05:00.434
Yeah, it looks like somebody
went a little too hard

00:05:00.434 --> 00:05:01.667
for National Wine Day.

00:05:01.667 --> 00:05:03.000
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:05.868
Hey, I heard about a couple
with a busy life

00:05:05.868 --> 00:05:08.901
who just got married
after a 60-year engagement.

00:05:08.901 --> 00:05:11.567
[ Ohs and laughter ]
Sixty years.

00:05:11.567 --> 00:05:13.367
That explains why one
of the gifts on the registry

00:05:13.367 --> 00:05:14.367
was a new hip.

00:05:14.367 --> 00:05:17.234
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:17.234 --> 00:05:18.501
It really is a sweet story.

00:05:18.501 --> 00:05:20.133
They actually met on the show

00:05:20.133 --> 00:05:21.701
"22,000 Day Fiancé."

00:05:21.701 --> 00:05:23.467
[ Laughter ]
It was really cute.
It's awesome.

